{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1091084-solar-historography","id":1091084,"title":"Solar Historography","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-11T05:47:40-07:00","id":1091084,"title":"Solar Historography","content":"I've argued before that the exact division of &quot;Ages&quot; is subjective and is likely a matter of debate and a telling note of a celestial god's politics, etc. That being the case, running with an idea in Dreams of the First Age, here is the Five Age model of Solar rule.<br /> <br /> Dawn Age: Begins with first Solar Exaltations and carries through the Primordial War and the conquests of Creation by the Primordials War veterans that followed. The rule of warriors, generals, and warlords.<br /> <br /> Zenith Age: Begins with the formation of the Deliberative and covers the &quot;height&quot; of their rule and the rule of Solar God Kings held together by faith in the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Twilight Age: Decline of Solar rule culminating in the Usurpation. The rule of faith gives way to the rule of Savants reshaping Creation and beyond to their will. While some obviously point to experimental abuses of mortals as defining the era, it was also a time of the height of &quot;First Age&quot; crafts and sorcery changing quality of life.<br /> <br /> Night Age: Usurpation till the return of the Solar Host. Period of shadows and guerilla resistance.<br /> <br /> Eclipse Age: The present. The Solar Host return to a world diverse and fractured and new alliances and societies must be built to take back what is theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:53:56-07:00","id":1091104,"title":"","content":"I like it and it does fit the narrative from the Solar's current point of view.<br /> <br /> That leads me to a possible flaw. Are the Solar ages circular, similar to the Wheel of Time. What comes after the Eclipse age, do we start over with the Dawn age and thus something catastrophic like another Usurpation will occur in the future? Will the Solar wane over time and the Lunar/Siderial/Abysal/ etc. age follow? Will the return of Autochthon start the ages in new and interesting directions?<br /> <br /> The current ages do not imply a circular nature or even and end of times while the Solar ages can imply both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>while (horse.state == dead)<br /> {<br /> beat();<br /> }","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/830-amdramnar","name":"Amdramnar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:13:47-07:00","id":1091112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1091084-solar-historography#post1091084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've argued before that the exact division of &quot;Ages&quot; is subjective and is likely a matter of debate and a telling note of a celestial god's politics, etc. That being the case, running with an idea in Dreams of the First Age, here is the Five Age model of Solar rule.<br /> <br /> Dawn Age: Begins with first Solar Exaltations and carries through the Primordial War and the conquests of Creation by the Primordials War veterans that followed. The rule of warriors, generals, and warlords.<br /> <br /> Zenith Age: Begins with the formation of the Deliberative and covers the &quot;height&quot; of their rule and the rule of Solar God Kings held together by faith in the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Twilight Age: Decline of Solar rule culminating in the Usurpation. The rule of faith gives way to the rule of Savants reshaping Creation and beyond to their will. While some obviously point to experimental abuses of mortals as defining the era, it was also a time of the height of &quot;First Age&quot; crafts and sorcery changing quality of life.<br /> <br /> Night Age: Usurpation till the return of the Solar Host. Period of shadows and guerilla resistance.<br /> <br /> Eclipse Age: The present. The Solar Host return to a world diverse and fractured and new alliances and societies must be built to take back what is theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the first point, the old devs saw fit to nuke that entire line of discussion from orbit. The Usurpation was a cataclysm that cost the world much. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3, pg 20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Solars were murdered and their Essences sealed away in a jade prison\u2014for such was their power that they could reincarnate upon death. But some escaped this initial ambush, and in the decades that followed the survivors waged terrible wars against the host of the usurpers. During that time, much of the magic of the First Age was lost\u2014expended or destroyed in cataclysmic acts of revenge. In time, the last of the Solars were hunted down and killed, and with them died the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the rest, I'm not sure you can helpfully divide the &quot;good&quot; part of the First Age into faith-based rule and the &quot;bad&quot; part of the First Age into knowledge-based rule. I see the &quot;technological&quot; arc as continuing essentially constantly the whole way through. If anything, Night would represent the Age of Nightmares, where Solar madness and tyranny has snuffed the light from the First Age.<br /> <br /> And there, unfortunately, I can't help but feel the model breaks down. The Usurpation feels more like a renewal of the Cycle than anything else, which makes sense; Exalted is ripped from the traditional stories of Titans and gods killing and usurping each other. In this case, it's the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded, and their &quot;Dawn&quot; is their violent overthrow of the Lawgivers.<br /> <br /> And they aren't even blessed with a Zenith period:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without the Solars to steady the sorcerous mechanisms that ran their world, the Realm began to disintegrate. This was no slow winding down, but the agonal throes of a beast mortally wounded. Cities collapsed. Manses rained brimstone on farmlands. Mountains buried themselves, dragging down nations with them. Whole islands were blasted from the seas as the sorceries that<br /> birthed them unwound themselves. The Sidereals, allies to the Dragon-Blooded, helped to steady the world against the First Age\u2019s dying. In the end, the world survived, yet it was vastly reduced. </div> </div> </div>The book has little to say about the Shogunate, except that it wasn't as awesome as the First Age, but wasn't rule by wacko birds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:33:23-07:00","id":1091119,"title":"","content":"I need to stress, I'm talking about historography, not objective truth. The SOLARS generally aren't going to see the Usurpation as a renewal of the cycle. From their perspective, it was the unprecedented downturn that they're only now coming back up from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-11-2017, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T12:30:26-07:00","id":1091226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1091084-solar-historography?p=1091119#post1091119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to stress, I'm talking about historography, not objective truth. The SOLARS generally aren't going to see the Usurpation as a renewal of the cycle. From their perspective, it was the unprecedented downturn that they're only now coming back up from.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a subjective, in-setting demarcation, this makes more sense. My only question then is who actually has the kind of sweeping knowledge of history in order to create something like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:24:18-07:00","id":1091248,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think subjectively Solars are going to have a wide range of rather different historiographical views, depending on the culture they were raised in, where they learned about history, what their first-age memories are like, etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Solars are far too varied (and for the most part, too poorly-educated in pre-Usurpation history) to have one view of history.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T15:43:04-07:00","id":1091306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1091084-solar-historography?p=1091226#post1091226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only question then is who actually has the kind of sweeping knowledge of history in order to create something like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI've got an image now of savants in the Realm who have decent access to unabridged Immaculate Texts such that they've got a fairly elaborate knowledge of at least the broad outlines, and compose heterodox alternate histories in secret as a form of intellectual dissent. I have a vague impression that it was the kind of thing that could happen in certain periods of Chinese history, particularly during the Qing Dynasty.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd then at some point the literature gets out, either as a deliberate act by some of those guerrilla historians trying to promulgate their work and their views, or on occasions in which they die and their personal effects get pillaged or sold off and whomever gets them manages to find the text among it and gets inspired.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd they start forming underground literary circles that gather under cover of just being societies for appreciation of incense burning, that are dedicated to lively discussion of just what the progression of history was like and debating the finer points of each solar phase era and how far they extend to each.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd the dissenting intellectual tradition combined with the organised group effort can form the core of a movement that actually intends insurrection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T11:39:37-07:00","id":1091638,"title":"","content":"Sounds interesting, like the kind of thing the Cult of the Illuminated would teach their Solar charges. <br /> <br /> I would like to make the new era, the resurgence of the Solars, equate to Dawn and the idea of them returning to Creation after a long absence. It just fits so nicely. But then we have to figure out where the Eclipse is in this as it's always can awkward one. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the idea that, just as Eclipses can happen at any time, Eclipses are singular moments that bring chaos or change and usher in the new era rather than an era themself. Every new era begins and ends with an Eclipse. The Usurpation itself was an Eclipse event that can be said to represent the end of the Twilight Era and the beginning of the Night era. The end of the Dawn era and the beginning of the Zenith Era was punctuated by the formation of the and acceptance of the Deliberate by the Exalted host.<br /> <br /> I like the basic idea and will probably see about finding a way to incorporate it into the next Cult of the Illuminated game I try to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}